    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Running a function"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Let's rewrite our previous function first."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "1#include <iostream>\n2using namespace std;\n3\n4void greet() {\n5    cout << \"Hello\" << endl;\n6    cout << \"How do you do?\";\n7}\n8\n9int main() {\n10\n11    return 0;\n12}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "If you run this code, you will not see any output. It's because creating a function doesn't mean we are executing the code inside it."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "It means the code is there for us to use if we want to. Now, we need to call (invoke) this function in order to use it."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Calling a Function in C++"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "We use the function name followed by parentheses to call the function."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "1#include <iostream>\n2using namespace std;\n3\n4void greet() {\n5    cout << \"Hello\" << endl;\n6    cout << \"How do you do?\";\n7}\n8\n9int main() {\n10\n11    greet();\n12\n13    return 0;\n14}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Hello\nHow do you do?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here's how this code works."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "When a function is called, the program control goes to the function definition, and then back to the function call",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "numbered_list",
      "items": [
        "When a function is called, the control of the program jumps to the function definition.",
        "Then, the statements inside the function are executed.",
        "After all the statements are executed, the control of the program jumps back to the function call and the next statement is executed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
